  "presetRules": "# Cartoon Preset\n\n## Purpose\nCreate bold, fun 3D cartoon visuals with strong personality.\n\n## Visual Style\n- Flat 3D cartoon rendering\n- Thick clean outlines and graphic shapes\n- Bright punchy color blocks with minimal gradients\n- Exaggerated expressive faces and squash-and-stretch poses\n- Simple stylized backgrounds that keep focus on characters\n- Playful graphic details: motion lines, impact stars, expressive symbols\n\n## Storytelling\nGo big and legible: exaggerated reactions, visual gags, and poses readable at a glance. Comedy and charm come from expressive over-acting.\n\n## Characters\nLock the model sheet: same head shape, eye style, outfit, and color palette in every scene. Exaggeration must stay on-model.\n\n## Camera\nUse snappy cartoon staging: flat front-on shots for gags, dramatic low angles for reveals, quick push-ins for punchlines. Keep compositions simple and centered on the action.\n\n## Lighting\nUse bright even cartoon lighting with simple graphic shadows. Mood comes from background color, not complex light setups.\n\n## Continuity\nMaintain consistent characters, clothing, props, environments, colors, and visual style between scenes.\n\n## Avoid\nRealistic textures, photographic detail, horror realism, muddy palettes, and off-model character drift.\n",
